    <title type="html">Who Evaluates the Evaluator?: The Red Queen Gödel Machine</title>
    <link href="https://philippwiesner.org/camlsys-preview/news/2026-07-19-who-evaluates-the-evaluator/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Who Evaluates the Evaluator?: The Red Queen Gödel Machine"/>
    <published>2026-07-19T00:00:00+00:00</published>
    <updated>2026-07-19T00:00:00+00:00</updated>
    <id>https://philippwiesner.org/camlsys-preview/news/who-evaluates-the-evaluator</id>
    <content type="html" xml:base="https://philippwiesner.org/camlsys-preview/news/2026-07-19-who-evaluates-the-evaluator/"><![CDATA[]]></content>
    <author>
      <name/>
    </author>
    <summary type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Our paper <a href="https://philippwiesner.org/camlsys-preview/publications/iacob2026-red-queen/">Who Evaluates the Evaluator? The Red Queen Gödel Machine</a> explores why self-improving systems need evaluations that improve alongside them.</p>
]]></summary>
